# Architecture of tailwind.config.js 🏗️

Every Tailwind project centers around `tailwind.config.js` (or `.ts` / `.mjs`).

```javascript_not
/** @type {import('tailwindcss').Config} */
module.exports = {
  content: [
    './index.html',
    './src/**/*.{js,ts,jsx,tsx,vue,svelte}',
  ],
  darkMode: 'class', // 'media' | 'class' | 'selector'
  theme: {
    extend: {
      // Your custom extensions live here!
    },
  },
  plugins: [],
};
```

## Core Properties
- `content`: Filepaths Tailwind scans for class names.
- `darkMode`: Configures how dark variants are triggered.
- `theme`: Customizes design tokens.
- `plugins`: Registers official and custom PostCSS plugins.

# Extending vs Overriding the Theme ⚖️

The placement of your customizations determines whether you preserve or replace Tailwind's default design tokens.

## 1. Extending the Theme (`theme.extend`)
Preserves all defaults and **adds** your custom values:

```javascript_not
module.exports = {
  theme: {
    extend: {
      colors: {
        brand: '#6366f1', // Keeps slate, blue, red, etc. and adds 'brand'!
      },
    },
  },
};
```

## 2. Overriding the Theme (`theme` directly)
Completely **wipes out** all default values for that key:

```javascript_not
module.exports = {
  theme: {
    colors: {
      brand: '#6366f1', // ONLY 'brand' exists! 'blue', 'gray', 'red' are GONE!
    },
  },
};
```

> ⚠️ **Best Practice:** In 95% of projects, always customize inside `theme.extend`!

# Custom Colors & CSS Variables 🎨

You can define static hex codes or integrate dynamic CSS custom properties.

## Defining Color Objects

```javascript_not
// tailwind.config.js
module.exports = {
  theme: {
    extend: {
      colors: {
        primary: {
          50: '#eef2ff',
          500: '#6366f1',
          900: '#312e81',
        },
        surface: 'var(--color-surface)',
      },
    },
  },
};
```

## Preserving Opacity with CSS Variables
If using CSS variables with Tailwind's `/opacity` syntax, format variables as space-separated RGB/HSL values:

```css_not
:root {
  --color-primary-rgb: 99 102 241;
}
```
```javascript_not
colors: {
  primary: 'rgb(var(--color-primary-rgb) / <alpha-value>)',
}
```

# Custom Fonts & Custom Spacing 📏

Augment typography and spacing to match Figma design specifications.

## Custom Font Stacks

```javascript_not
// tailwind.config.js
module.exports = {
  theme: {
    extend: {
      fontFamily: {
        display: ['Cabinet Grotesk', 'sans-serif'],
        body: ['Inter', 'system-ui', 'sans-serif'],
      },
      spacing: {
        '128': '32rem',   // w-128 = 512px
        '144': '36rem',   // h-144 = 576px
      },
    },
  },
};
```

Use them immediately: `font-display text-4xl w-128`.

# The @layer Directive Revisited 🗃️

Tailwind categorizes all generated CSS into three distinct layers to manage specificity:

1. **`base`**: Browser resets, typographic defaults, typography tag overrides.
2. **`components`**: Multi-class UI abstractions (`.card`, `.btn-primary`).
3. **`utilities`**: Single-purpose utility overrides.

```css_not
@layer components {
  .input-field {
    @apply w-full px-4 py-2 rounded-lg border border-gray-300 dark:border-gray-700 bg-white dark:bg-gray-800 text-gray-900 dark:text-white focus:ring-2 focus:ring-indigo-500 focus:outline-none transition-all;
  }
}
```

Classes defined in `@layer components` are automatically purged if unused in your template files!

# Authoring Custom Plugins 🔌

Plugins allow you to register new utilities, components, and variants programmatically with JavaScript.

## Creating a Utility Plugin

```javascript_not
// tailwind.config.js
const plugin = require('tailwindcss/plugin');

module.exports = {
  plugins: [
    plugin(function({ addUtilities, matchUtilities, theme }) {
      // Static custom utility
      addUtilities({
        '.scrollbar-none': {
          '-ms-overflow-style': 'none',
          'scrollbar-width': 'none',
          '&::-webkit-scrollbar': {
            display: 'none',
          },
        },
      });
    }),
  ],
};
```

# Dynamic Utilities with matchUtilities ⚡

Use `matchUtilities` to support theme values AND arbitrary square-bracket values automatically!

```javascript_not
const plugin = require('tailwindcss/plugin');

module.exports = {
  plugins: [
    plugin(function({ matchUtilities, theme }) {
      matchUtilities(
        {
          // Generates 'tab-size-2', 'tab-size-[4]', etc.
          'tab-size': (value) => ({
            'tab-size': value,
          }),
        },
        { values: theme('tabSize') }
      );
    }),
  ],
};
```

# Sharing Configurations with Presets 📦

In design systems and multi-repo organizations, define your theme once and share it across apps via `presets`.

```javascript_not
// tailwind.config.js (App Repo)
module.exports = {
  presets: [
    require('@company/design-system-tailwind-preset')
  ],
  content: ['./src/**/*.{html,js,jsx,ts,tsx}'],
  // You can still add app-specific overrides here
};
```

The preset can bundle brand colors, fonts, default plugins, and custom breakpoints into a single reusable npm package.

# The Safelist & Blocklist Options 🛡️

Tailwind's scanner purges any class that doesn't appear explicitly in source code. What if class names come from a database or external CMS?

## The `safelist` Option

Force Tailwind to generate specific classes even if not detected in template files:

```javascript_not
// tailwind.config.js
module.exports = {
  safelist: [
    'bg-red-500',
    'text-3xl',
    {
      pattern: /bg-(red|green|blue)-(100|500|900)/,
      variants: ['hover', 'focus'],
    },
  ],
};
```

## The `blocklist` Option
Prevent specific classes from ever being generated to enforce design system rules (e.g., blocking `blocklist: ['container']`).

# Architecture of a Real-World Design Token System 🏛️

Here is a complete, production-ready `tailwind.config.js` incorporating modern design system practices:

```javascript_not
const colors = require('tailwindcss/colors');

/** @type {import('tailwindcss').Config} */
module.exports = {
  content: ['./src/**/*.{html,js,ts,jsx,tsx}'],
  darkMode: 'class',
  theme: {
    extend: {
      colors: {
        primary: colors.indigo,
        secondary: colors.slate,
        accent: colors.emerald,
        surface: {
          light: '#f8fafc',
          dark: '#0f172a',
        },
      },
      borderRadius: {
        '4xl': '2rem',
      },
      boxShadow: {
        glow: '0 0 25px -5px rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.4)',
      },
    },
  },
  plugins: [
    require('@tailwindcss/forms'),
    require('@tailwindcss/typography'),
  ],
};
```
